*[[Nick Fury]] gives [[Phil Coulson]] the [[Bus]] before he is set to assemble his new team.{{Ref|AoS102}}<ref name="AoS101-109 Placement">In ''[[Pilot]]'', Grant Ward is promoted to Level 7 at S.H.I.E.L.D. and receives a new ID badge, with the issue date saying "[[:File:Ward Level 7 ID.jpg|2013SEP09]]," placing the events of the episode from September 8-12, 2013. At the end of ''[[0-8-4 (episode)|0-8-4]]'', Nick Fury tells Phil Coulson that it took him and his team "six days" to cause damage to the Bus. Coulson was given the Bus on September 8, 2013, positioning the episode around September 13-14, 2013. ''[[The Well]]'' picks up in the aftermath of ''[[Thor: The Dark World]]'', with Coulson's team helping clean up the damage caused during the Battle of Greenwich on November 17, 2013 (see other references), dating ''The Well'' to November 18-22, 2013 and ''[[Repairs]]'' to November 23, 2013, which picks up the following morning. The episodes in between ''0-8-4'' and ''The Well'' can thus be evenly distributed between September 14, 2013 and November 18, 2013, accounting for ''[[The Asset]]'' being said to partially occur during "the weekend" as well as ''[[FZZT]]'' beginning with a group of boy scouts camping, something which would make the most sense to occur on a Saturday, dating ''The Asset'' to September 25-28, 2013, ''[[Eye-Spy]]'' to October 6-9, 2013, ''[[Girl in the Flower Dress]]'' to October 16-18, 2013, ''FZZT'' to October 26-30, 2013, and ''[[The Hub]]'' to November 7-9, 2013.</ref>
