====15th====
*'''[[Liberation of Edison Po]]''': [[Edison Po]] is broken out of [[Havenworth Federal Penitentiary]] by [[Brian Hayward]] and other [[Centipede Soldiers]].{{Ref|AoS110}}<ref name="AoS110-112 Placement">''[[The Bridge]]'', ''[[The Magical Place]]'', and ''[[Seeds]]'' all take place some time between the events of ''[[Repairs]]'' on November 23, 2013 (see other references) and the events of ''[[T.R.A.C.K.S.]]'' on February 5, 2014 (see [[2014]] references), with ''The Magical Place'' taking place in the days following ''The Bridge''. The implied passage of time between episodes does not appear to be very long, with each episode appearing to be decently soon after the last. Evenly distributing these few episodes between ''Repairs'' and ''T.R.A.C.K.S.'' ends up placing the events of ''The Bridge'' and ''The Magical Place'' from December 15-19, 2013 and the events of ''Seeds'' from January 9-11, 2014. These dates end up working out quite nicely, as ''The Bridge'' and ''The Magical Place'' avoid occurring on Christmas, which would be strange for characters not to address if that were the case, and in ''Seeds'', during her lecture with Leo Fitz at S.H.I.E.L.D. Academy, Jemma Simmons states, "We tend to forget that these organizations... Hydra, Centipede, A.I.M.... were also made up of extremely brilliant scientists, men and women who started with the same unlimited potential as you or I." The implication from this is that A.I.M., being included in the same sentence as Hydra and Centipede, is openly known to corrupt and compromised, a fact that was exposed during the events of ''[[Iron Man 3]]'', meaning ''Seeds'' would have to occur after December 25, 2013 (see other refences). During said episode, Phil Coulson tells Skye that the Massacre in Hunan, which occurred around Spring 1989 (see [[1980s]] references), happened "24 years ago," potentially suggesting the episode occurs in 2013. However, this is impossible, as it has to occur after Christmas 2013 and it cannot be during the final few days of the year due to the term being in session at S.H.I.E.L.D. Academy, forcing the episode into 2014. ''Seeds'' being a few weeks after ''Iron Man 3'' in early to mid-January 2014 also allows enough time between the film and the episode for the aftermath of the film to settle and knowledge regarding A.I.M. to spread, as well as enough time into the term for a test to be given out as mentioned by Seth Dormer and Callie Hannigan early in the episode. Therefore, it must be taken that Coulson is either rounding down from 24.75 years for whatever reason, or is using Skye's thought-to-be age (24).</ref>
*Needing help tracking down the [[Centipede Project]], [[Phil Coulson]] travels to a [[S.H.I.E.L.D. Training Facility]] to recruit new [[S.H.I.E.L.D.]] trainee [[Mike Peterson]].{{Ref|AoS110}}<ref name="AoS110-112 Placement"/>
*[[Coulson's Team]] tracks down [[Laura Hayward]] and traces her cell phone call to Brian to [[Oakland]], [[California]].{{Ref|AoS110}}<ref name="AoS110-112 Placement"/>
*[[File:Mike Peterson and Phil Coulson.jpg|250px|thumb|[[Ambush at the Oakland Centipede Laboratory]]]]'''[[Ambush at the Oakland Centipede Laboratory]]''': Coulson, Peterson, [[Melinda May]] and [[Grant Ward]] lead an attack on the facility, not knowing that three Centipede soldiers were in cargo bins waiting to strike. They were deployed to attack the S.H.I.E.L.D. agents. Peterson gets stabbed by a stick causing him severe damage, but despite the injury, he manages to subdue Hayward. May also takes another Centipede soldier down, but he manages to escape with another soldier. Before being interrogated, Hayward is killed using his [[Backscatter X-Ray Eye Implant]].{{Ref|AoS110}}<ref name="AoS110-112 Placement"/>
