**Inside, he discovers the Mandarin who appears on television is actually an actor, [[Trevor Slattery]], who is oblivious to the actions carried out in his name.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
**The Mandarin is a creation of [[Aldrich Killian]], who appropriated [[Maya Hansen]]'s [[Extremis]] as a cure for his own disabilities and expanded the program to include injured war veterans.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
*[[File:Stark-MockedByKillian-IM3.jpeg|thumb|250px|[[Tony Stark]]'s life is threatened by [[Aldrich Killian]]]]Killian captures Stark and reveals he has also kidnapped [[Pepper Potts]]. To gain Stark's aid in fixing Extremis' flaws, Killian injects Potts with it. <ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
*Hansen has a change of heart about Killian's plans, but she gets murdered by him.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
*'''[[Kidnapping of President Ellis]]''':
**[[Aldrich Killian]] has also manipulated American intelligence agencies regarding the [[Trevor Slattery|Mandarin]]'s location, luring the [[Iron Patriot]] into a trap to steal the armor.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
**Stark escapes and reunites with Rhodes, discovering Killian's plan to attack U.S. President [[Matthew Ellis]] aboard [[Air Force One]].<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
**Disguised in the Iron Patriot armor, [[Eric Savin]] infiltrates Air Force One and detonates an explosive.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
**[[File:Tonyandheather.png|thumb|250px|[[Tony Stark]] saves the passengers]]Remotely controlling the Mark XLII armor, Stark saves some surviving passengers and crew, but cannot stop Killian from abducting Ellis. They trace them to an impounded oil tanker, the ''[[Norco]]'', where Killian intends to kill Ellis on live television.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
**[[United States Secret Service]] sends an immediate message saying that [[Iron Patriot]] has gone rogue and kidnapped President [[Matthew Ellis]]. Vice President [[Gil Rodriguez]] is now in command.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="TWFATEotAaB"/>
**The Vice President [[Gil Rodriguez]] (who is secretly working for Killian) will become a puppet leader, following Killian's orders in exchange for Extremis to cure his daughter's disability.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}

====25th====
*'''[[Battle on the Norco]]''':
**On the platform of the ''[[Norco]]'', [[Tony Stark]] goes to save [[Pepper Potts]], while [[James Rhodes]] rescues the President.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
**[[File:Iron Legion.jpg|thumb|250px|The [[Iron Legion]] arrives]]Stark summons the [[Iron Legion]], controlled remotely by [[J.A.R.V.I.S.]], to provide air support, and discovers Pepper has survived the [[Extremis]] procedure. However, before he can save her, a rig collapses around them and she falls to her apparent death.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
**Stark confronts [[Aldrich Killian]], traps him in the [[Iron Man Armor: Mark XLII|Mark XLII]] and sets it to self-destruct, but it fails to kill him. Pepper, whose Extremis powers allowed her to survive her fall, intervenes and kills Killian.<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}
**After the battle, Stark promises to devote more time to Pepper, and orders [[J.A.R.V.I.S.]] to remotely destroy every armor in the Iron Legion. Vice President [[Gil Rodriguez]] and [[Trevor Slattery]] are arrested, ending [[Aldrich Killian's False Flag Attacks]].<ref name="Iron Man 3Source"/><ref name="CACWP"/>{{Ref|IM3}}

====31st====
*[[Carl Lucas]] and [[Squabbles]] take some time for themselves. They go down to the ring and Lucas proceeds with his training.<ref name="LC104 Flashbacks"/>{{Ref|LC104}}

==Behind the Scenes==
*In the comic ''[[w:c:marvel:Young Avengers Vol 2 8|Young Avengers Vol 2, Issue 8]]'', the [[w:c:marvel:Young Avengers|Young Avengers]] from [[w:c:marvel:Earth-616|Earth-616]] traveled across the [[w:c:marvel:Multiverse|Multiverse]] in order to find their missing teammate, [[w:c:marvel:Speed|Speed]]. They arrived at Earth-199999, which is the official designation for the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] within Marvel's multiverse system. Adding this into the MCU's continuity, the [[w:c:marvel:Young Avengers|Young Avengers]] would have arrived on June 16, 2013, but, after not finding [[w:c:marvel:Speed|Speed]], they would have continued their search travelling to [[w:c:marvel:Earth-8765|Earth-8765]] the following day (June 17th).<ref name="YA">''[[w:c:marvel:Young Avengers Vol 2 8|Young Avengers Vol 2, Issue 8]]''</ref><ref name="YATR">[https://imgur.com/giHC9O3 Young Avengers' date of visit on Earth-199999]</ref>

